---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Terms of Use | Infinilink Broadband" 
  description="Terms of Use and Service Agreement for Infinilink Broadband services in Wise County, Texas."
>
  <div class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-slate-950 text-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-slate-800 pb-8 mb-12">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-400 border border-cyan-800 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
          Legal Agreement
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
          Terms of Use & Service
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
          Last Updated: March 2026 • Infinilink Broadband (Runaway Bay & Decatur, TX)
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content Sections -->
      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-slate max-w-none space-y-10 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        
        <section class="bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Overview</h2>
          <p>
            This website and related telecommunications services are operated by Infinilink Broadband ("Infinilink", "we", "us", and "our"). 
            Infinilink offers this website, including all information, tools, and services available from this site to you, the user, 
            conditioned upon your acceptance of all terms, conditions, policies, and notices stated here.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            By visiting our site, purchasing service, or subscribing to our high-speed broadband network, you engage in our "Service" and agree 
            to be bound by the following terms and conditions ("Terms of Service", "Terms"), including any additional terms and policies 
            referenced herein or available by hyperlink.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 1 – Online Terms & Eligibility</h2>
          <p>
            By agreeing to these Terms of Service, you represent that you are at least the age of majority in your state of residence, 
            or that you have given us your consent to allow any of your minor dependents to use this site. You may not use our services 
            or equipment for any illegal or unauthorized purpose, nor may you violate any laws in your jurisdiction (including but not 
            limited to copyright, network integrity, and telecommunication laws).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 2 – General Conditions & Service Provision</h2>
          <p>
            We reserve the right to refuse service to anyone for legitimate operational or network integrity reasons at any time. 
            Fixed wireless broadband is subject to physical line-of-sight propagation, terrain clearance, and radio frequency interference factors. 
            Our field service technicians evaluate line-of-sight viability before finalizing any residential or commercial installation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 3 – Network Performance & Truly Unlimited Policy</h2>
          <p>
            Infinilink residential broadband packages come with zero data caps and zero throttling. We do not enforce artificial monthly data limits, 
            overage billing, or post-threshold bandwidth penalties. Customers enjoy truly unlimited data across all plan tiers. 
            All network usage remains subject to acceptable use practices prohibiting harmful network disruptions, denial-of-service activities, or illegal redistribution.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 4 – Modifications to Service & Pricing</h2>
          <p>
            Prices for our monthly service plans are subject to change with advance written notice to subscribers. We reserve the right at any time 
            to update or discontinue specific service packages or features. We shall not be liable to you or any third party for modifications, 
            suspensions, or discontinuance of promotional offers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 5 – Billing, Payments & Customer Portal</h2>
          <p>
            Service billing is managed directly through our secure online billing portal at 
            <a href="https://billing.infinilinkbroadband.com" class="text-cyan-400 underline font-semibold hover:text-cyan-300" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              billing.infinilinkbroadband.com
            </a>. 
            Subscribers are responsible for keeping credit card, payment details, and contact information up-to-date. Invoices are generated monthly on a recurring schedule.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 6 – Equipment, Installation & Property Access</h2>
          <p>
            Standard residential installations include an outdoor fixed wireless transceiver/antenna, mounting bracket, exterior rated ethernet cabling, 
            and an indoor Power-over-Ethernet (POE) injector. Subscribers grant Infinilink technicians reasonable access to the property for site surveys, 
            installation, signal alignment, and maintenance. Infinilink-owned hardware remains the property of Infinilink and must be returned in good working condition upon service termination.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 7 – Month-to-Month Flexibility & Contract Options</h2>
          <p>
            Standard residential plans operate on a flexible month-to-month basis with no mandatory long-term contracts. Subscribers may cancel service at any time without early termination penalties. Where promotional free or discounted upfront installation is selected in exchange for an agreed term contract, the terms of that specific promotional agreement shall apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 8 – Return & Refund Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We stand behind our local service. If you experience technical service issues during your initial installation period, contact us immediately at (940) 437-0550 so our field crew can inspect or realign your connection. For customer-purchased hardware returns, items must be in original condition with proof of purchase within 30 days.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 9 – Prohibited Uses</h2>
          <p>
            You are prohibited from using the service or network: (a) for any unlawful purpose; (b) to transmit unauthorized commercial spam or bulk automated traffic; (c) to infringe upon intellectual property rights; (d) to transmit malware, viruses, or destructive code; (e) to attempt unauthorized access to other network accounts or infrastructure; or (f) to engage in activities that degrade service quality for other subscribers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Section 10 – Limitation of Liability & Governing Law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service and any separate agreements whereby we provide you Services shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Texas, with venue in Wise County, Texas.
          </p>
          <p>
            While Infinilink maintains a reliable network with triple fiber backhauls (including 100% uptime over the last 90 days), internet transmissions may occasionally experience temporary interruptions due to severe weather, power outages, upstream carrier disruptions, or scheduled maintenance. In no event shall Infinilink, its officers, or staff be liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from connection downtime.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Contact & Mailing Block -->
        <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl mt-10">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Questions or Official Inquiries?</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm mb-4">
            For questions regarding these Terms of Service or your account, reach out to our local team:
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm text-slate-300">
            <div>
              <p class="font-bold text-white">Infinilink Broadband</p>
              <p>101 Cooper Ct</p>
              <p>Runaway Bay, TX 76426</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p><strong class="text-white">Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:9404370550" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">(940) 437-0550</a></p>
              <p><strong class="text-white">Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@infinilinkbroadband.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">support@infinilinkbroadband.com</a></p>
              <p><strong class="text-white">Customer Portal:</strong> <a href="https://billing.infinilinkbroadband.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">billing.infinilinkbroadband.com</a></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
